meta {
  name: Bulk Edit OPD Panels
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/opd-master-data/{{opdMasterDataId}}/opd-panels/bulk
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "data": [
      {
        "opdPanelId": "{{opdPanelId}}",
        "isActive": false,
        "turnaroundPriority": "STAT",
        "isDisableDiscount": true,
        "commissionPrice": 210
      },
          {
        "opdPanelId": "{{opdPanelId}}",
        "isActive": false,
        "turnaroundPriority": "STAT",
        "isDisableDiscount": true
      }
    ]
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  opdPanelId: 7304fcdc-3c2a-4ee9-9837-7bbde89ca922
  opdMasterDataId: 3bebbd8d-eef4-4bfa-88f3-3aff4a4a4516
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("reports updated count", function () {
    const data = res.getBody() && res.getBody().data;
    expect(data).to.have.property("updated");
  });
}

docs {
  OPD equivalent of the lab **Bulk Edit Lab Panels** endpoint (PATCH /opd-master-data/:masterDataId/opd-panels/bulk).
  
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires `business_admin:master_data__allow_multiple_edit` — enforced by `PermissionGuard` (`@RequirePermission`). A caller whose effective permissions (user override ?? branch-role override ?? role baseline) lack this get **403 `PERMISSION_DENIED`**; the `business_admin` / `administrator` roles bypass all checks, so `{{businessAccessToken}}` (an admin) still succeeds here.
  
  Bulk-edit lab panels: `data` is an array of per-panel edits, each carrying its
  own `opdPanelId` plus the scalar fields to change **for that panel** (scoped to
  the caller's tenant + the path's master data). Only the panels in the payload
  are touched. Returns `{ updated: <count> }`.
  
  ## Rules
  
  - `data` — 1 to 500 items. Each item's `opdPanelId` must resolve to an active
    panel in this master data; an unresolved id → 404 `LAB_PANEL_NOT_FOUND`.
  - Each item may set any subset of the panel's **scalar** fields (classification,
    applicability, reporting, status, pricing, TAT, flags, `maxTestsRemovable`).
    `panelName`/`panelCode` and the `tests` composition are **not** bulk-editable
    — use the single-panel update for those.
  - **All-or-nothing**: duplicate `opdPanelId`s, an item with no changes, or a
    broken cross-field invariant (re-checked per panel against its existing values
    + test count) → 422 `VALIDATION_ERROR` and **nothing** is changed. Updates run
    in one transaction.
}
